    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d845">

                <pb facs="0748" n="736" sameAs="frus:frus1942v04/pg736"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">867.24/389: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Turkey</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Steinhardt</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Istanbul</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1942-08-20T12:00:00+03:00">August 20,
                            1942—noon</date>.<lb/>[Received 1:40 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>47. Department’s 95, August 17. I have today communicated to the Prime Minister
                    substance of Department’s cable under reference.</p>
                <p>In connection with a visit made to Ankara and Istanbul by Jackson, head of the
                    MESC, and Fred Winant,<anchor n="64" xml:id="d845-f1"/> I had occasion to
                    discuss with them the delivery of the 15,000 tons of wheat. Jackson stated that
                    he expected to be able to deliver 5,000 tons by September 15 and 5,000
                    additional tons by October 15 but that the delivery to Turkey of the final 5,000
                    tons would be dependent upon the arrival in the Middle <pb facs="0749" n="737"
                        xml:id="pg737"/> East of the first of the shipments from the United States
                    sent in replacement of the 10,000 tons already advanced by the MESC.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Steinhardt</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d845-f1" n="64" xml:id="d845-f1-content">
                <p>American representative on the Middle East Supply Center.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
